1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,344
Chapter six — running it.

2
00:00:03,404 --> 00:00:12,553
A static diagram cannot show you
where the traffic actually goes.

3
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:22,558
Play run moves packets along the
real edges, at the modelled rates.

4
00:00:22,618 --> 00:00:36,240
Thicker, busier links are carrying more.
That is the diurnal profile, played back.

5
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:55,826
Half speed to study it, four
times to watch a whole day go by.

6
00:00:55,886 --> 00:01:02,312
Arrange lays the graph out
again when it gets messy.

7
00:01:02,372 --> 00:01:11,192
Underneath is the analysis
panel — six tabs, always live.

8
00:01:11,252 --> 00:01:22,567
Bottlenecks: what is saturated,
and the number that says so.

9
00:01:22,627 --> 00:01:34,447
Costs: per node, per month,
at the current workload.

10
00:01:34,507 --> 00:01:46,533
Network: what each link carries
and what crossing a domain costs.

11
00:01:46,593 --> 00:01:57,439
Events: what the run produced, in order.

12
00:01:57,499 --> 00:02:08,966
Capacity: ceilings and headroom, node by node.

13
00:02:09,026 --> 00:02:19,788
And Ask, for a question about
the design in plain English.

14
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:23,590
Nothing here is a report you asked for.

15
00:02:23,650 --> 00:02:27,853
It is the state of the design, at all times.
